<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arminius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 17 BCE – 21 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arminius was a chieftain of the Germanic Cherusci who had served in the Roman army. In 9 CE he led an alliance of Germanic tribes that destroyed three Roman legions under Varus in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutoburg-forest">Teutoburg Forest</a>. The defeat halted Roman efforts to conquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arminius.jpg" alt="Arminius" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Schwen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermannsdenkmal_statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
